        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "63f1e0e7-356b-57bf-ac9d-79e2871b0add",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Iphigénie en Tauride, Der Barbier von Bagdad, Chimène\n- People: Christoph Willibald Gluck, Peter Cornelius, Nicolas-François Guillard\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, tragédie lyrique, One Thousand and One Nights\n\nFacts:\n- Iphigénie en Tauride is a 1779 opera in four acts by Christoph Willibald Gluck.\n- Nicolas-François Guillard’s most famous work is Iphigénie en Tauride, which was his first libretto.\n- Christoph Willibald Gluck initially rejected Nicolas-François Guillard’s libretto for Iphigénie en Tauride before later setting it.\n- Der Barbier von Bagdad is a comic opera in two acts by Peter Cornelius.\n- Peter Cornelius wrote the German libretto for Der Barbier von Bagdad himself.\n- Der Barbier von Bagdad is based on “The Tale of the Tailor” and “The Barber’s Stories of his Six Brothers” from One Thousand and One Nights.\n- Chimène is a tragédie lyrique in three acts.\n- Nicolas-François Guillard wrote the libretto for Chimène.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
